  "plain": "Ronald Reagan's diary entry for June 11, 1985 reads, as Michels quotes it: \"I learned that our shuttle capacity is such we could orbit 300 people.\" Michels brings this up himself on two episodes, also saying that Reagan's 1980s diaries mention meetings with top astronomers from NASA. He reads it as a hint of a space program much bigger than the public knew. The line itself states a shuttle capacity and leaves open what it was for or whether it was ever used."
